ax": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "coarsely chopped canned plum tomatoes with ½ cup juice reserved", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "2 tablespoons chopped fresh basil", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "chopped fresh basil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "1 ½ teaspoons chopped fresh rosemary", "group": null, "quantity": 1.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "chopped fresh rosemary", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "2 tablespoons water", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "water", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 12, "raw": "2 tablespoons chopped fresh Italian parsley", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "chopped fresh italian parsley", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 13, "raw": "Salt and freshly ground black pepper to taste", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "salt and freshly ground black pepper to taste", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 14, "raw": "1 cup lightly toasted bread crumbs", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "lightly toasted bread crumbs", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 15, "raw": "6 thin slices hearty country-style bread, toasted", "group": null, "quantity": 6.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "thin slices hearty country-style bread", "preparation": "toasted", "optional": false}, {"position": 16, "raw": "1 pound fresh jumbo sea scallops, rinsed, muscle removed and each sliced horizontally into 3 thin rounds", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "lb", "item": "fresh jumbo sea scallops", "preparation": "rinsed, muscle removed and each sliced horizontally into 3 thin rounds", "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Cut 6 rounds, ½ inch thick, from the eggplant. Place on paper towels and sprinkle with 1 teaspoon salt. Let stand for 1 hour. Peel the remaining eggplant and cut into small dice. In a large, heavy skillet, heat 1 tablespoon of the olive oil over medium-high heat. Add the diced eggplant and cook until the edges begin to brown. Remove from the pan and place on a baking sheet to cool. Repeat with the zucchini and then the yellow squash, adding oil as needed. Remove from the pan and set aside."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Add 2 tablespoons olive oil to the pan. Add the onions and garlic and cook for 2 minutes. Add the tomatoes and reserved juice. Lower the heat and add the herbs. Cook 5 minutes. Transfer the sauce to a bowl and wipe the pan dry. Add 2 tablespoons of oil to the pan and heat over medium heat. Place the eggplant rounds and water in the oil and brown evenly, about 3 to 5 minutes per side. Remove from the pan and let cool."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Preheat the oven to 350 degrees. Stir the diced vegetables and 1 tablespoon of parsley into the tomato mixture. Season to taste with salt and pepper. Stir the remaining parsley into the bread crumbs. Place the bread slices on a baking sheet and top each one with an eggplant round. Spoon the vegetable mixture over the eggplant slices. Place the scallop slices over the sauce, overlapping them slightly. Top with the bread crumbs. Bake until the scallops contract and the bread crumbs are brown, about 15 to 20 minutes. Divide among 6 plates and serve."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 405.4, "protein_g": 16.0, "carbohydrates_g": 42.3, "fat_g": 20.5, "saturated_fat_g": 3.0, "trans_fat_g": 0.0, "cholesterol_mg": 18.1, "sodium_mg": 915.0, "fiber_g": 7.2, "sugar_g": 9.4, "unsaturated_fat_g": 16.3, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["french"], "diet": [], "course": ["main course"], "meal": ["dinner"], "occasion": [], "other": ["bake", "casseroles", "eggplant", "saute", "scallop", "zucchini"]}, "images": [], "rating": null, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "1993-03-21", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T01:29:33.190216+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "provencal-tomato-and-squash-gratin", "nyt_id": 12681, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/12681-provencal-tomato-and-squash-gratin", "name": "Provençal Tomato and Squash Gratin", "author": "Martha Rose Shulman", "description": "Some of the tomatoes in this gratin are cooked down to a savory sauce, while the rest are sliced and used to decorate the top.", "servings": {"text": "6 servings", "min": 6, "max": 6, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 105, "raw": {"total": "1 hour 45 minutes"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "2 pounds tomatoes", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "lb", "item": "tomatoes", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "2 tablespoons extra virgin olive oil", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "extra virgin olive oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "2 large garlic cloves, minced", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "large garlic cloves", "preparation": "minced", "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "½ medium or 1 small onion", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "medium or 1 small onion", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "½ pound summer squash (1 good-size zucchini, for example), cut in ½-inch dice", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "lb", "item": "summer squash (1 good-size zucchini", "preparation": "for example), cut in ½-inch dice", "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "Salt and freshly ground pepper to taste", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "salt and freshly ground pepper to taste", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "2 teaspoons fresh thyme leaves, or 1 teaspoon crumbled dried thyme", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "fresh thyme leaves", "preparation": "or 1 teaspoon crumbled dried thyme", "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "1 cup cooked rice, farro or barley", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "cooked rice", "preparation": "farro or barley", "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "3 eggs", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "eggs", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "2 ounces Gruyère cheese, grated (½ cup)", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "oz", "item": "gruyère cheese", "preparation": "grated (½ cup)", "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "1 to 2 tablespoons slivered or chopped fresh basil leaves", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": 2.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "slivered or chopped fresh basil leaves", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Peel and seed half the tomatoes, and chop fine. Slice the rest and set aside. Preheat the oven to 375 degrees. Oil a 2-quart gratin or baking dish."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Heat 1 tablespoon of the olive oil in a large, heavy nonstick skillet over medium heat. Add the onion and cook, stirring often, until it is translucent, about 5 minutes. Add the garlic, stir together for about 30 seconds, until it begins to smell fragrant, and stir in the squash. Cook, stirring often, until the squash is translucent, about 5 minutes. Add the chopped tomatoes and the thyme, season with salt and pepper, raise the heat slightly and cook, stirring often, until the tomatoes have cooked down and smell fragrant, 10 to 15 minutes. Stir in the rice or other grains and remove from the heat."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Beat the eggs in a large bowl. Stir in the cooked vegetables, salt and pepper to taste, and the cheese and combine well. Scrape into the gratin dish."}, {"position": 4, "text": "Slice the remaining tomatoes and cover the top of the gratin in one layer. Drizzle on the remaining tablespoon of olive oil. Bake 45 minutes, or until the top is browned and the gratin is sizzling. Remove from the heat and allow to sit for at least 10 minutes before serving. Sprinkle the basil over the top. Serve hot, warm or at room temperature."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 191.7, "protein_g": 8.8, "carbohydrates_g": 16.5, "fat_g": 10.7, "saturated_fat_g": 3.5, "trans_fat_g": 0.0, "cholesterol_mg": 92.1, "sodium_mg": 608.4, "fiber_g": 2.8, "sugar_g": 5.3, "unsaturated_fat_g": 6.5, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["french"], "diet": ["gluten-free", "healthy", "low-sodium", "vegetarian"], "course": ["side dish"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["bake", "rice", "saute", "squash", "summer", "tomato"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2012/08/14/science/14recipehealth/14recipehealth-facebookJumbo-v2.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": true}], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 1087}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2012-08-14", "scraped_at": "2026-09-06T23:59:08.230874+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
